    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d403">

                <pb facs="0392" n="276" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg276"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 437.00/24.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to the
                            Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 86.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Habana</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-01-30">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 30, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to previous
                        correspondence<anchor n="1" xml:id="d403-f1"/> in regard to the so-called
                    Cuban “insurrectionary claims,” I have the honor to report <pb facs="0393"
                        n="277" xml:id="pg277"/> that the question is apparently receiving serious
                    attention from the Cuban Government.</p>
                <p>I understand that in the course of a day or two President Gómez is to begin a
                    series of conferences with members of the various interested committees of the
                    Cuban Congress, with his Cabinet, and with leaders of different political
                    parties and factions. * * *</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">A. M. Beaupré</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
